            <ArticleTitle>Difficult Airway Management Caused by Local Anesthetic Allergy During Emergent Cesarean Delivery: A Case Report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>84-86</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1213/XAA.0000000000000533</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Difficult airway management in the gravid patient is a well-described phenomenon. We present a case of emergent cesarean delivery complicated by a &quot;cannot intubate, cannot ventilate&quot; scenario that was later determined to be secondary to an allergic, IgE-mediated reaction to epidurally administered local anesthetic.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
